Tasks covered: radicands, nonzero denominators, and both endpoint checks.

- **a)** \(x\ge0\), \(x+1\ge0\), and \(\sqrt{x+1}-5\ne0\).
  The last excludes \(x=24\). Domain:
  **\([0,24)\cup(24,\infty)\)**.
  At 0 the denominator is \(-4\) and \(y=0\), so 0 is included.
- **b)** \(-x\ge0\) and \(x+10\ge0\) give \(-10\le x\le0\).
  The denominator \(1+\sqrt{x+10}\ge1\) never vanishes.
  Domain: **\([-10,0]\)**. At \(-10\), \(y=\sqrt{10}\); at 0, \(y=0\).

